torch._int_mm (int8 x int8 -> int32) always fails on gfx803. On ROCm,
at::cuda::blas::int8_gemm calls hipBLASLt and has no other path, and
hipBLASLt has never shipped kernels for gfx803. The heuristic query finds no
TensileLibrary_lazy_gfx803.dat and returns HIPBLAS_STATUS_INVALID_VALUE:

  rocblaslt error: Cannot read ".../hipblaslt/library/TensileLibrary_lazy_gfx803.dat"
  RuntimeError: CUDA error: HIPBLAS_STATUS_INVALID_VALUE when calling
  `hipblasLtMatmulAlgoGetHeuristic( ltHandle, ...`

TORCH_BLAS_PREFER_HIPBLASLT=0 does not help, because int8_gemm never asks
for the preferred backend. The fp gemm, bgemm and addmm paths already check
getHipblasltSupportedArchs() and fall back to rocBLAS. int8_gemm is the one
caller in this file that does not. Anything that quantizes a linear layer to
int8 reaches it, for example ComfyUI's comfy_kitchen int8 backend. To
reproduce, run torch._int_mm on two 1024x1024 int8 CUDA tensors.

With this patch, int8_gemm calls rocblas_gemm_ex (i8 inputs, i32 output and
compute) on any arch outside getHipblasltSupportedArchs(). It uses the same
handle, stream and column-major contract as the fp16 rocblas_gemm_ex call
earlier in this file. The arch check comes first, so archs that hipBLASLt
supports keep the Lt path unchanged. rocBLAS ships I8I_HPA Tensile kernels
for gfx803 in all four transpose layouts. Called directly on an RX 570, they
matched a CPU reference bit for bit on 32 cases: 8 shapes from 17x8x8 to
2048x6144x2048, each in NN, NT, TN and TT.

Verified on an RX 570 with this patch built into torch 2.14 at two
release/2.14 commits, 245c136 and c299f65: torch._int_mm matches a CPU
reference bit for bit on 5 shapes from 17x8x8 to 4096x4096x64, each with
plain, transposed-A and transposed-B inputs. Those are the 15 cases that
failed without the patch. The c299f65 run used the published final image as
CI built it, with nothing installed over it.

gfx803 has no int8 dot instruction, so these kernels are not fast. They reach
about 1.56 TOPS at 2048^3 and larger, half of fp16 matmul on the same card
(3.1 TFLOPS). On this card int8 saves memory but does not add speed.

--- a/aten/src/ATen/cuda/CUDABlas.cpp
+++ b/aten/src/ATen/cuda/CUDABlas.cpp
@@ -2090,6 +2090,61 @@
   return;
 }
 
+#ifdef USE_ROCM
+// GFX803_INT8_GEMM_ROCBLAS_PATCH: hipBLASLt ships no kernels for archs outside
+// getHipblasltSupportedArchs(), so on those the Lt heuristic query below fails
+// with HIPBLAS_STATUS_INVALID_VALUE. rocBLAS carries int8 -> int32 Tensile
+// kernels for them, with the same column-major contract as the Lt call.
+static void int8_gemm_rocblas(
+    bool transpose_mat1,
+    bool transpose_mat2,
+    int64_t m,
+    int64_t n,
+    int64_t k,
+    const int8_t* mat1_ptr,
+    int64_t mat1_ld,
+    const int8_t* mat2_ptr,
+    int64_t mat2_ld,
+    int32_t* result_ptr,
+    int64_t result_ld) {
+  CUDABLAS_NONNEGINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, m);
+  CUDABLAS_NONNEGINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, n);
+  CUDABLAS_NONNEGINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, k);
+  CUDABLAS_POSINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, mat1_ld);
+  CUDABLAS_POSINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, mat2_ld);
+  CUDABLAS_POSINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, result_ld);
+  cublasHandle_t handle = at::cuda::getCurrentCUDABlasHandle();
+  CUBLAS_SM_CARVEOUT_GUARD(handle);
+  int32_t alpha = 1;
+  int32_t beta = 0;
+  TORCH_CUDABLAS_CHECK(rocBLASStatusToHIPStatus(rocblas_gemm_ex(
+      (rocblas_handle)handle,
+      transpose_mat1 ? rocblas_operation_transpose : rocblas_operation_none,
+      transpose_mat2 ? rocblas_operation_transpose : rocblas_operation_none,
+      m,
+      n,
+      k,
+      &alpha,
+      mat1_ptr,
+      rocblas_datatype_i8_r,
+      mat1_ld,
+      mat2_ptr,
+      rocblas_datatype_i8_r,
+      mat2_ld,
+      &beta,
+      result_ptr,
+      rocblas_datatype_i32_r,
+      result_ld,
+      result_ptr,
+      rocblas_datatype_i32_r,
+      result_ld,
+      rocblas_datatype_i32_r,
+      rocblas_gemm_algo_standard,
+      0,
+      0)));
+}
+#endif
+
 void int8_gemm(
     bool transpose_mat1,
     bool transpose_mat2,
@@ -2102,6 +2157,15 @@
     int64_t mat2_ld,
     int32_t* result_ptr,
     int64_t result_ld) {
+#ifdef USE_ROCM
+  if (!at::detail::getCUDAHooks().isGPUArch(
+          at::detail::getCUDAHooks().getHipblasltSupportedArchs())) {
+    int8_gemm_rocblas(
+        transpose_mat1, transpose_mat2, m, n, k,
+        mat1_ptr, mat1_ld, mat2_ptr, mat2_ld, result_ptr, result_ld);
+    return;
+  }
+#endif
 
   cublasComputeType_t computeType = CUBLAS_COMPUTE_32I;
   cudaDataType_t scaleType = CUDA_R_32I;
